  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Scaling up Access to Prevention, Treatement and Care under the National Program for Prevention and Control of HIV/AIDS/STIs 2006-2010 and reducing morbitidy, mortality and HIV-related impact on people living with HIV/AIDS, 2010-2014 - Moldova (01-Jan-2015-31-Dec-2017)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Moldova is experiencing a concentrated HIV epidemic with an overall prevalence of less than 1 percent. The program supported by this grant aims to reduce sexual and mother-to-child transmission of HIV and other sexually transmitted infections and the transmission of HIV via needle sharing by scaling up access to voluntary counseling and testing services, and expanding prevention interventions for vulnerable groups. In addition, social and health services for people living with HIV will be expanded and activities will be undertaken to combat stigma and discrimination.</narrative>
  </description>
